<title>USA: John Hancock settles lawsuit for $350 mln.</title>
<headline>John Hancock settles lawsuit for $350 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>John Hancock Mutual Life Insurance Co on Friday said it resolved a class-action lawsuit and will offer policyholders a &quot;wide array of relief and benefits&quot; totaling about $350 million.</p>
<p>The settlement, which covers about 3.7 million life insurance policies sold from 1979 through 1996, will have &quot;no material impact&quot; on the company's financial health, John Hancock said.</p>
<p>The suit involved allegations about the company's sales practices, John Hancock said.</p>
